\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces CMA-ES exploration of the four potential parameters at fixed $R_e$ and $J$, for the drainhole (top) and symmetric (bottom) families. Panels (a,b,d,e) project recorded proposals, coloured by evaluation order; diamonds mark each search's lowest $X$ with both background-constraint residuals below $10^{-6}$. The $q_3$ axes are symmetric-logarithmic, linear for $|q_3|\le 1$. Panels (c,f) show the running minimum relative to the first candidate below that threshold. The searches concentrate in distinct parameter regions and approach plateaus at different rates.}}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:search-regions}{{3}{4}{CMA-ES exploration of the four potential parameters at fixed $R_e$ and $J$, for the drainhole (top) and symmetric (bottom) families. Panels (a,b,d,e) project recorded proposals, coloured by evaluation order; diamonds mark each search's lowest $X$ with both background-constraint residuals below $10^{-6}$. The $q_3$ axes are symmetric-logarithmic, linear for $|q_3|\le 1$. Panels (c,f) show the running minimum relative to the first candidate below that threshold. The searches concentrate in distinct parameter regions and approach plateaus at different rates}{figure.3}{}}
